mika: quick a11y pass on query-builder chips (filter tokens). Issues: chip close X low contrast, keyboard focus on chips skips between groups, screen reader labels read only 'button' for chip.

ash: repro steps? which AT/browser?

mika: Chrome+NVDA. Tab into chip list, NVDA says 'button' with no context; pressing ArrowRight doesn't move focus between chips, and the X icon is #9aa0a6 on white (hard to see).

a11y-bot: Automated contrast check: #9aa0a6 on #ffffff => 2.9:1 (FAIL for UI control).

clair: recommendations: 1) expose semantic list container (<ul role="list">) with <li role="listitem"> for chips, 2) make the remove control a native <button> with an explicit aria-label (e.g., "Remove filter: status open"), 3) restore :focus-visible styles and avoid outline:none, 4) support arrow key navigation between chips.

owen: small CSS/JS snippets:

CSS:
.chip .remove { color: #1f2d3a; /* meets contrast */ }
.chip:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #ffd166; outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 4px; }

JS (concept):
const chips = container.querySelectorAll('.chip button');
chips.forEach((btn,i)=>{
  btn.setAttribute('aria-label', `Remove filter ${btn.dataset.label}`);
  btn.addEventListener('keydown', (e)=>{
    if(e.key === 'ArrowRight') chips[(i+1)%chips.length].focus();
    if(e.key === 'ArrowLeft') chips[(i-1+chips.length)%chips.length].focus();
  });
});

mika: will add axe run and manual NVDA check in PR. TL;DR: semantic list, explicit aria-labels, higher contrast for X, visible focus, and arrow-key navigation. I'll open a small PR and tag @clair for review. :raised_hands:
